# 2026-11-25 — status tables are written by HQL

How to change anything under `doc/status/`. Decided with the user on
2026-11-25, when the first tracker moved its rows into data. The full
description of the files is [the status page](../status/index.hmd).

Progress is not tracked here. This note records how the trackers are edited.

## The rule

Do not type into a table that an HQL cell wrote. Change the data the cell
reads, then run `hql render`, and commit the data and the rendered output
together.

A table was written by a cell when it sits between an `<!-- hql:output … -->`
marker and an `<!-- /hql:output -->` marker. The next render replaces
everything between those markers, so a hand edit there is lost.

## A tracker whose rows are data

[`hmd.hmd`](../status/hmd.hmd) is the first tracker of this kind. Its rows are
a list named `work` in the frontmatter of the card. To add, change, or remove
a row:

1. Edit the row in the `work` list. Each row has a `kind` (`open`, `broken`,
   `limitation`, `done`, or `question`), a `state` on `open` and `broken`
   rows, `tags`, `text`, and optionally `notes` and `refs`.
2. Render the tracker and the views that read it, from the repository root:

   ```sh
   hql render --in-place --emit after doc/status/hmd.hmd doc/status/kanban.hmd doc/status/proposals.hmd doc/status/open.hmd
   ```

3. Run `hmd lint` from `doc/`. The rendered tables are part of the card, so
   the linter checks the references in them.

A row that cites a proposal for the first time also needs an import in the
frontmatter, such as `from /proposals/HMD-0032 import index as hmd-0032`.

## A tracker that still has hand-written tables

`lang.hmd`, `ts-core.hmd`, `vsc-ext.hmd`, `rs-core.hmd`, `semantics.hmd`, and
`pages.hmd` have not moved yet. Their tables have no output markers, and they
are edited by hand as before. After an edit to an Open row, run the same
command without `doc/status/hmd.hmd`, so that the open-work view follows.

Check which kind a tracker is before editing it: a tracker with a `work` list
in its frontmatter is of the first kind. The plan is to move the other six the
same way, one at a time.

## The three views

`kanban.hmd`, `proposals.hmd`, and `open.hmd` are queries over the whole
vault. Never edit them except to change a query. Render them in the same
commit that moves an issue, changes the status of a proposal, or changes an
Open row.

## HQL 0.8.0 or later

`hql render` needs HQL 0.8.0 or later in this vault. Earlier versions do not
read `location_path` from `doc/.hmd/config.toml` and refuse to run. The pinned
toolchain in `toolchain.json` still ships 0.7.2 as of 2026-11-25, so use an
`hql` installed with `cargo install hql`.

## Asking a question of the trackers

The same data answers questions without opening a file. Run a query from
`doc/`, for example the open rows that carry the tag `lsp`:

```sh
hql eval 'type Row { kind : String, state? : String, tags : List<String>, text : String, notes? : String, refs? : String }
type Tracker : Data { work? : List<Row> }

cards
| flat_map(c => match (c.header | Tracker).work { some(rows) => rows, _ => [] })
| filter(r => r.kind == "open" and (r.tags | any(t => t == "lsp")))
| map(r => { state: r.state.unwrap_or(""), work: r.text })
| Table(columns = ["state", "work"])
| format(as = Markdown)'
```

A query of this kind sees only the trackers whose rows are data.
